CHANGES
T-L6 review (diff 9292a527..HEAD). Re-ran `flutter test test/features/profiles`: 135/135 pass. Copy matches 04-UI-UX A6-A9 and 03-APP-FLOW §10.1 word for word; error text comes from the code only; one primary button; tokens only (LD-140); no logging or storage of code, link or PHI; paths stay inside apps/patient_app. Backend items (RLS, permissions, rate tier) are not touched by this UI task.

1. apps/patient_app/lib/features/profiles/profiles_api.dart:4, :60-67 (also profiles_screen.dart:4): E18 `updateMyProfile` and E19 `removeMyProfile` send no `If-Match`. contracts/openapi/engagement.yaml:987 and :1080 reference `_common.yaml#/components/parameters/IfMatch`, which is `required: true` (_common.yaml:92). The TRD (02-TRD.md:447-448) also lists If-Match. A compliant server answers 428 `common.precondition_required` to every call, so Change relationship and Remove (US-EN-06.4) can never work. The writer's "open point" is not a CR, and there is no `.orchestra/cr/T-L6*.md`. Fix: write `.orchestra/cr/T-L6.md` using the template in spec/program/04-CHANGE-REQUESTS.md. Gap: `Profile` has no `version`, but E18/E19 require If-Match. Options: add `version` to Profile, or make If-Match optional on E18/E19. Include the second gap in the same CR: US-EN-05.2 "link earlier visits" has no wire flag. Once the lead rules, add `version` to `ProfileItem` and send `If-Match: "<version>"` on E18/E19.
2. apps/patient_app/integration_test/profiles_prism_test.dart is missing. The task brief asks for "widget + integration_test", and .orchestra/notes/T-L6-tests.md lists this file, but it is not in the diff or in git history. Only sign_in_prism_test.dart exists. Fix (tester): add the file, following sign_in_prism_test.dart, covering E13 list, E14 redeem, E15 redeem and E16+E17 register against Prism. Put the run command in its header. Correct T-L6-tests.md if the scope changes.
3. apps/patient_app/lib/features/profiles/register_screen.dart:322-329: 04-UI-UX A9 says "Myself (disabled if a `self` profile exists)". Here, Myself still looks selectable and a tap is silently ignored (`if (v == 'self' && _hasSelf) return;`). Fix: render the Myself option disabled, using LimsSegmentedControl's disabled or enabled option if it has one. If the component has no such option, raise it in the CR from item 1 instead of faking it. Add a widget test that the option is disabled when E13 has a `self` profile.
